##

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.170 line:91%
A few months ago,
I did parkour up in Scotland,

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:06.916 line:91%
and I made the mistake of
just absent-mindedly saying...

00:00:06.916 --> 00:00:09.608 line:91%
...that, "Oh, I wanna try
tightrope now!"

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.739 line:85%
This is Chris!

00:00:12.419 --> 00:00:13.506 line:85%
<c.yellow>Hello!</c>

00:00:13.506 --> 00:00:17.197 line:85%
The Bullzini Family Circus Yard?

00:00:17.197 --> 00:00:20.296 line:91%
<c.yellow>Circus Yard, that's where you are,
and tightrope is my thing.</c>

00:00:20.296 --> 00:00:23.801 position:69% line:91%
<c.yellow>So you've definitely come to the right place
if you wanna try tightrope.</c>

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:27.223 position:70% line:91%
Is "tightrope" the right word?
'Cause I've heard "highwire" and all sorts...

00:00:27.223 --> 00:00:29.015 line:85%
<c.yellow>You can call it what you like.</c>

00:00:29.015 --> 00:00:33.720 line:85%
<c.yellow>It's a tensioned steel wire rope,</c>

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.194 line:85%
<c.yellow>which is high.</c>

00:00:36.194 --> 00:00:40.854 position:63% line:91%
<c.yellow>So the reason why we call it "highwire",
as opposed to "tightwire",</c>

00:00:40.854 --> 00:00:43.852 line:91%
<c.yellow>or "dance wire" they
sometimes call a lower wire,</c>

00:00:43.852 --> 00:00:46.086 line:85%
<c.yellow>is because of the height obviously.</c>

00:00:46.086 --> 00:00:48.867 line:91%
<c.yellow>So it's a slightly different
mental and physical training.</c>

00:00:48.867 --> 00:00:51.507 line:85%
<c.yellow>So how are you with heights, Tom?</c>

00:00:51.507 --> 00:00:53.669 line:85%
I— I'm fine with heights!

00:00:53.669 --> 00:00:56.041 line:85%
Falling, not so much.

00:00:56.041 --> 00:00:57.933 line:91%
<c.yellow>It's not the falling.
It's not even the falling.</c>

00:00:57.933 --> 00:01:00.879 line:91%
<c.yellow>It's more of the landing
that can be dangerous.</c>

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:02.950 line:85%
Yeah, yeah, you're fine(!)

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.582 position:63% line:85%
The first twenty metres will be great(!)

00:01:04.582 --> 00:01:06.767 line:91%
<c.yellow>Exactly, just enjoy it.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Just the bit at the end...</c>

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:10.503 line:91%
<c.yellow>The plan is not to drop you
on the ground. That's my job.</c>

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.859 position:58% line:85%
<c.yellow>So don't worry. You're in safe hands.</c>

00:01:12.859 --> 00:01:18.140 position:64% line:91%
<c.yellow>But there is definitely a lot about
the mental process of preparing yourself.</c>

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:22.568 position:77% line:91%
<c.yellow>So that's what I wanna do with you, is to get you
feeling really calm and really grounded.</c>

00:01:22.568 --> 00:01:26.182 line:91%
<c.yellow>Having a healthy respect
for heights and an awareness</c>

00:01:26.182 --> 00:01:29.142 line:91%
<c.yellow>that you don't want your body
to fall off and hit the ground.</c>

00:01:29.142 --> 00:01:31.050 line:85%
<c.yellow>For me, that's sane.</c>

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:33.980 line:85%
<c.yellow>That's not being wimpy or foolish.</c>

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.806 line:91%
<c.yellow>That's actually really sensible
and really sane.</c>

00:01:36.806 --> 00:01:39.482 line:91%
<c.yellow>And that's why
the technique, the training,</c>

00:01:39.482 --> 00:01:42.836 line:91%
<c.yellow>and the safety harness in this case
are really essential.</c>

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:44.342 line:85%
<c.yellow>To, you know...</c>

00:01:44.342 --> 00:01:46.739 line:85%
<c.yellow>We're not as crazy as we look!</c>

00:01:48.929 --> 00:01:52.305 position:63% line:91%
I don't know what to expect here.
I don't know the height of what we're...

00:01:52.305 --> 00:01:54.560 line:85%
Oh, that is— That— <i>(laughs)</i>

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.379 line:85%
<c.yellow>That's the height basically.</c>

00:01:56.379 --> 00:01:58.066 line:85%
I saw Penn and Teller once.

00:01:58.066 --> 00:02:00.001 line:91%
<c.yellow>Ah yeah.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>And they were doing—</c>

00:02:00.001 --> 00:02:03.278 position:66% line:91%
Something that stuck in my head
was the phrase that the trick is the same,

00:02:03.278 --> 00:02:06.712 line:91%
whether the rope is
one foot off the ground...

00:02:06.712 --> 00:02:08.046 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>...or...</c>

00:02:08.046 --> 00:02:10.194 line:91%
...gonna guess about
30 feet off the ground?

00:02:10.194 --> 00:02:13.062 position:59% line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah, it's actually a little bit less.
So it's already less than...</c>

00:02:13.062 --> 00:02:14.943 line:91%
Okay! Okay!
<c.yellow>...than you're worried about.</c>

00:02:14.943 --> 00:02:16.445 line:91%
<c.yellow>Eight metres.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Eight metres, okay.</c>

00:02:16.445 --> 00:02:19.836 line:91%
It's "serious injury" territory
if you come off, though, isn't it?

00:02:19.836 --> 00:02:22.581 position:83% line:91%
<c.yellow>Well it won't be for you, 'cause you'll be connected.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Obviously not, but...</c>

00:02:22.581 --> 00:02:25.066 position:63% line:91%
<c.yellow>It would be for me,
because I work without a safety harness.</c>

00:02:25.066 --> 00:02:29.399 line:91%
<c.yellow>But yeah, it's really not about
the F word.</c>

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:33.182 position:63% line:91%
<c.yellow>And in fact, your training starts there.
Don't mention the F word.</c>

00:02:33.182 --> 00:02:34.486 line:85%
Okay.

00:02:34.486 --> 00:02:39.161 line:91%
<c.yellow>It's really not about that—
What we always have to do is</c>

00:02:39.161 --> 00:02:43.309 line:91%
<c.yellow>step onto the wire,
and be present on the wire,</c>

00:02:43.309 --> 00:02:46.063 line:91%
<c.yellow>with the confidence
that we're in control,</c>

00:02:46.063 --> 00:02:49.709 line:91%
<c.yellow>and we choose when
we're gonna get off the wire.</c>

00:02:50.276 --> 00:02:55.348 position:61% line:91%
<c.yellow>So really visualising that, really
establishing that in your mind's eye...</c>

00:02:55.348 --> 00:02:59.095 line:91%
<c.yellow>that's where it starts,
is believing that you can do it.</c>

00:02:59.095 --> 00:03:03.272 position:69% line:91%
Normally at this point, I would have kind of
some sarcastic or self-deprecating—

00:03:03.272 --> 00:03:06.252 position:58% line:91%
But I'm not, I'm gonna buy into this,
'cause I'm gonna be up there soon!

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.410 line:91%
<c.yellow>Cool.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Absolutely.</c>

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:12.259 line:91%
I'm not gonna mention the F word.
I'm gonna walk across there.

00:03:12.259 --> 00:03:14.369 line:85%
<c.yellow>Great, great, great, great.</c>

00:03:14.369 --> 00:03:16.969 position:58% line:85%
<c.yellow>Well, that's the place to start from.</c>

00:03:16.969 --> 00:03:20.089 position:61% line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah, I believe you can do it,
so you know, that's at least one of us.</c>

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:25.900 align:start size:88% position:13% line:7%
<c.cyan><i>♪ (tense ticking music)</i></c>

00:03:32.224 --> 00:03:35.726 line:91%
How do you do that? How on earth
do you balance like that?

00:04:10.374 --> 00:04:12.644 line:85%
<i>(heavy sigh, clapping)</i>

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.000 align:start size:88% position:13% line:7%
<c.cyan><i>(music fades)</i></c>

00:04:13.762 --> 00:04:16.724 line:91%
<c.yellow>So, we're not going to
start you up there.</c>

00:04:16.724 --> 00:04:19.178 line:91%
<c.yellow>We're gonna start you
on something much safer and lower</c>

00:04:19.178 --> 00:04:21.490 line:85%
<c.yellow>just down here.</c>

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:24.114 line:85%
<c.yellow>So if you wanna come this way,</c>

00:04:24.114 --> 00:04:26.242 position:61% line:85%
<c.yellow>I'm just gonna put the final tension on</c>

00:04:26.242 --> 00:04:28.542 line:85%
<c.yellow>to make sure that it's about right.</c>

00:04:28.542 --> 00:04:31.180 line:85%
<c.yellow>Just do that on this little device,</c>

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:34.133 line:85%
<c.yellow>and that should be good like that.</c>

00:04:34.752 --> 00:04:37.127 line:91%
Oh! <i>(laughs)</i>
<c.yellow>So here's your balance pole.</c>

00:04:37.127 --> 00:04:40.553 line:91%
That's... That's good.
That's got— That's got—

00:04:40.553 --> 00:04:43.583 position:56% line:91%
It's wide. There's a lot of balance
available here is what I'm thinking.

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:46.031 line:91%
<c.yellow>It's very long.
It is actually a shorter one.</c>

00:04:46.031 --> 00:04:48.661 line:91%
<c.yellow>Come and have a feel
of the pole on the ground.</c>

00:04:48.661 --> 00:04:49.607 line:85%
'Kay.

00:04:49.607 --> 00:04:51.509 line:91%
<c.yellow>Then I shall talk us through
some of the technique</c>

00:04:51.509 --> 00:04:53.591 line:85%
<c.yellow>before we get you onto the wire.</c>

00:04:53.591 --> 00:04:54.159 line:85%
Okay.

00:04:54.159 --> 00:04:56.672 line:91%
It's— It's heavier than
I thought it was gonna be.

00:04:56.672 --> 00:04:58.763 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yeah, that's what people
always say.</c>

00:04:58.763 --> 00:05:01.127 position:58% line:85%
<c.yellow>This one is about eight to ten kilos.</c>

00:05:01.127 --> 00:05:02.224 line:85%
...Alright!

00:05:02.224 --> 00:05:05.380 position:67% line:91%
<c.yellow>So how you hold it,
if you bring your hands a little bit wider,</c>

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:09.033 position:73% line:91%
<c.yellow>bring the flat of your palms,
so your fingers are not even gripped around it.</c>

00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:11.401 line:91%
<c.yellow>That's it. That's better.
And then bring it up</c>

00:05:11.401 --> 00:05:14.033 line:91%
<c.yellow>so that the middle of it is,
yeah, around your belly, good.</c>

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:15.815 line:91%
<c.yellow>Now pull your elbows in
towards your body,</c>

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:17.768 line:91%
<c.yellow>and dropping your shoulders
down the back.</c>

00:05:17.768 --> 00:05:19.703 line:85%
<c.yellow>Okay, now that is much better.</c>

00:05:19.703 --> 00:05:21.282 line:91%
Oh, okay!
<c.yellow>A little bit wider in the hands.</c>

00:05:21.282 --> 00:05:22.870 line:91%
<c.yellow>A little bit wider.
Okay, cool.</c>

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:26.744 line:91%
<c.yellow>So what I want is that
your fingers don't have to hold on.</c>

00:05:26.744 --> 00:05:30.796 line:91%
It feels more like I've got a thing
just resting in each palm.

00:05:30.796 --> 00:05:32.384 line:85%
<c.yellow>Yeah, to start with, yes.</c>

00:05:32.384 --> 00:05:35.048 line:91%
<c.yellow>If you need to wrap
the fingers around, you can.</c>

00:05:35.048 --> 00:05:37.035 line:91%
<c.yellow>Put it down if you
need to rest your arms for a bit.</c>

00:05:37.035 --> 00:05:40.691 line:91%
Yeah, I think I'll save the...
save the muscles.

00:05:40.691 --> 00:05:42.831 line:91%
<c.yellow>Again, just pat the arms out,
massage out,</c>

00:05:42.831 --> 00:05:44.669 line:91%
<c.yellow>'cause you'll be getting
a lot of tension doing this.</c>

00:05:44.669 --> 00:05:47.304 position:69% line:91%
It's heavier than I thought it was gonna be.
<c.yellow>Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.</c>

00:05:47.304 --> 00:05:50.444 position:69% line:91%
<c.yellow>So let me show you.
I'll show you first of all without the pole.</c>

00:05:50.444 --> 00:05:51.757 line:85%
Okay.

00:05:51.757 --> 00:05:57.121 align:start position:0% line:91%
<c.yellow>And if you want to just watch,
and you can almost imagine yourself,</c>

00:05:57.121 --> 00:06:00.095 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<c.yellow>if you like, you can
imagine yourself being me.</c>

00:06:01.007 --> 00:06:04.330 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<c.yellow>And just be aware that
when the feet get on,</c>

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:07.964 align:start position:0% line:91%
<c.yellow>the correct foot position is for
the big toe to be over the wire,</c>

00:06:07.964 --> 00:06:11.604 line:91%
<c.yellow>and then through
the middle of the heel at the back.</c>

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:15.808 position:56% line:91%
<c.yellow>And when you stand up onto the wire,
you'll have the pole,</c>

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:17.930 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<c.yellow>but I'm just gonna balance
with my hands.</c>

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:21.214 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<c.yellow>And then, my teacher in Cuba
used to say like this, it goes,</c>

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:25.652 align:start size:97% position:3% line:85%
<c.yellow><i>dedo, deslizar, talón, paso.</i></c>

00:06:25.821 --> 00:06:29.408 align:start size:97% position:3% line:85%
<c.yellow><i>Dedo, deslizar, talón, paso.</i></c>

00:06:29.408 --> 00:06:33.109 line:91%
So that's touch, forward—
<c.yellow>Toe, slide,</c>

00:06:33.109 --> 00:06:35.008 line:85%
<c.yellow>heel, step.</c>

00:06:35.008 --> 00:06:39.252 line:91%
<c.yellow>That's right.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Toe, slide, heel, step.</c>

00:06:39.252 --> 00:06:40.036 line:85%
<c.yellow>Yeah.</c>

00:06:40.036 --> 00:06:43.713 line:91%
<c.yellow>So what we're doing with the eyes,
we're looking at a fixed point.</c>

00:06:45.236 --> 00:06:50.169 position:56% line:91%
<c.yellow>And the best fixed point to look at
is the point at the end of the wire,</c>

00:06:50.169 --> 00:06:53.227 line:91%
<c.yellow>because... that's where
we want to arrive.</c>

00:06:53.227 --> 00:06:55.654 line:91%
<c.yellow>Let's start with the feet.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yep.</c>

00:06:55.654 --> 00:06:58.666 line:85%
<c.yellow>And I can help you with the pole.</c>

00:06:58.975 --> 00:07:00.641 line:91%
Alright, so...
<c.yellow>So...</c>

00:07:00.641 --> 00:07:03.673 line:91%
<c.yellow>If you hold that, and if
you remember the centre...</c>

00:07:03.673 --> 00:07:05.505 line:91%
Open palm.
<c.yellow>Open palm.</c>

00:07:05.505 --> 00:07:07.538 line:91%
On the belly just there,
tucked in.

00:07:07.538 --> 00:07:09.141 line:91%
<c.yellow>I'm going to support this,
so we don't have to worry too much</c>

00:07:09.141 --> 00:07:10.349 line:85%
<c.yellow>about balancing to start with.</c>

00:07:10.349 --> 00:07:12.855 position:56% line:91%
Okay.
<c.yellow>'Cause we wanna get those feet good.</c>

00:07:12.855 --> 00:07:14.838 line:91%
<c.yellow>If you need to fall off...</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yeah?</c>

00:07:14.838 --> 00:07:16.974 line:91%
<c.yellow>I'll just show you this
if you stand there for a second.</c>

00:07:16.974 --> 00:07:19.004 line:91%
<c.yellow>There are two ways
to leave the wire,</c>

00:07:19.004 --> 00:07:21.225 position:58% line:85%
<c.yellow>if you really have to leave the wire.</c>

00:07:21.225 --> 00:07:23.544 line:91%
<c.yellow>One way, which is not advisable,
is like that.</c>

00:07:23.544 --> 00:07:26.027 line:91%
Yes! I have made that mistake
once in my life

00:07:26.027 --> 00:07:28.384 line:91%
on a slackline in a park,
and it hurt!

00:07:28.384 --> 00:07:29.998 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yes!</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Yup.</c>

00:07:29.998 --> 00:07:34.423 position:69% line:91%
<c.yellow>You only need to do that once
to realise that that's the way not to do it.</c>

00:07:34.423 --> 00:07:37.651 line:91%
<c.yellow>So being really aware that
if you do need to leave the wire,</c>

00:07:37.651 --> 00:07:40.998 line:91%
<c.yellow>then to go one side
or the other.</c>

00:07:40.998 --> 00:07:45.008 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<c.yellow>Magic. When you're ready,
come up with the other foot.</c>

00:07:45.008 --> 00:07:47.495 align:start position:0% line:91%
<c.yellow>Stand up tall and straight.
Bring the pole up to your belly.</c>

00:07:47.495 --> 00:07:49.768 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<c.yellow>Good. Keep looking
at the end of the wire.</c>

00:07:49.768 --> 00:07:52.257 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<c.yellow>Both feet on the wire.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Oh, that's got a wobble on!</c>

00:07:52.257 --> 00:07:55.680 align:start position:0% line:91%
I've got a wobble. Nope, back down.
<c.yellow>Breathe, breathe. OK, OK, OK.</c>

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.090 line:85%
Wow! That— That moves...

00:07:59.074 --> 00:08:00.396 line:85%
That moves a lot. Okay.

00:08:00.396 --> 00:08:03.003 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<c.yellow>If you're really wobbly,
the wire will wobble.</c>

00:08:03.003 --> 00:08:06.061 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<c.yellow>So if you can use your breath
to calm your body...</c>

00:08:06.061 --> 00:08:08.627 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<i>(breathes deeply)</i>
<c.yellow>That's it. Super cool.</c>

00:08:08.627 --> 00:08:10.362 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<c.yellow>Super cool.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Toe on the wire.</c>

00:08:10.362 --> 00:08:13.229 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<c.yellow>Toe on the wire.
When you're ready, allez-hup.</c>

00:08:13.729 --> 00:08:15.853 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
<c.yellow>Great.
And other foot on the wire.</c>

00:08:16.518 --> 00:08:17.480 align:start size:97% position:3% line:85%
<c.yellow>Good.</c>

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:19.849 align:start position:0% line:91%
<c.yellow>Okay, breathe. Pull the pole to your belly.</c>
<i>(titters)</i>

00:08:19.849 --> 00:08:22.547 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yep, pull up a bit.
Elbows into the body.</c>

00:08:22.547 --> 00:08:25.170 line:91%
<c.yellow>Cool, and when you're ready,
step forward.</c>

00:08:25.592 --> 00:08:26.858 align:start size:97% position:3% line:85%
<c.yellow>And try to slide—</c>

00:08:26.858 --> 00:08:28.928 align:start size:97% position:3% line:91%
Wheeey!
<c.yellow>Okay, you got it, you got it.</c>

00:08:28.928 --> 00:08:30.667 align:start position:0% line:85%
<c.yellow>Stand up straight. Stand strong.</c>

00:08:30.667 --> 00:08:32.495 line:91%
Hang on, no. I lost that.
<c.yellow>Okay, okay, okay.</c>

00:08:32.495 --> 00:08:34.470 line:91%
<i>(laughs)</i> Okay.
<c.yellow><i>(laughs)</i></c>

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:36.437 position:56% line:85%
<c.yellow>If you need to lean onto the pole...</c>

00:08:36.437 --> 00:08:40.125 line:91%
Yeah.
<c.yellow>So this is the next step.</c>

00:08:40.125 --> 00:08:42.558 line:91%
<c.yellow>We're gonna try a bit
of this now.</c>

00:08:42.558 --> 00:08:45.700 line:91%
<c.yellow>So when you get up
onto the wire with the pole,</c>

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:49.665 line:91%
<c.yellow>And if you feel like
you need to fall off,</c>

00:08:49.665 --> 00:08:51.800 line:91%
<c.yellow>you just rest the pole down.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Oh, I can just rest the pole down!</c>

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.992 line:91%
<c.yellow>Yep. And just rest the pole down.</c>
<c.colorEEEEEE>Okay!</c>

00:08:53.992 --> 00:08:55.716 line:85%
I can't do that up there!

